      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A patient who sustained a posterior shoulder subluxation injury after being positioned in the lateral decubitus head-down position during emergence from general anesthesia is presented. It is postulated that the injury occurred as a result of violent retching while in the lateral position."},
